  "text": "PetCure Oncology Dallas Fort Worth Advanced Cancer Care for Pets\nPetCure Oncology\nPet Parents: Get Help Now!\nVeterinarians: Refer A Patient\nSearch\nSearch PetCure Oncology\nCancel\nCall us at\n833-738-4376\nPet Cancer\nPet Cancer In Dogs\nPet Cancer In Cats\nPet Cancer Treatment Options\nMaking A Pet Cancer Treatment Decision\nPet Cancer Treatment\nStereotactic Radiation (SRS/SRT) Treatment FAQ\nWhat Makes Us Different?\nWhat To Expect from Treatment\nMedical Oncology\nTelehealth\nClinical Trials & Research\nPayment Resources\nLocations\nPetCure Chicago\nPetCure Clifton, NJ\nPetCure Dallas Fort Worth\nPetCure Phoenix\nPetCure Pittsburgh\nPetCure San Antonio\nPetCure San Jose\nTraveling For Cancer Treatment\nPet Stories\nPet Parent Stories\nShare Your Pet Story\nFor Vets\nRefer a Patient\nComplimentary Imaging Reviews\nAbout Radiation Oncology\nPrimary Care Veterinarians\nB-Cell Lymphoma in Dogs\nNon-Cancerous Conditions\nPost Surgical Radiation\nClinical Information\nCase Studies\nNon-Urgent Questions\nVeterinary FAQ\nAbout\nHistory & Mission\nClinical Leadership\nBusiness Leadership\nContact\nPet Cancer\nPet Cancer In Dogs\nPet Cancer In Cats\nPet Cancer Treatment Options\nMaking A Pet Cancer Treatment Decision\nPet Cancer Treatment\nStereotactic Radiation (SRS/SRT) Treatment FAQ\nWhat Makes Us Different?\nWhat To Expect from Treatment\nMedical Oncology\nTelehealth\nClinical Trials & Research\nPayment Resources\nLocations\nPetCure Chicago\nPetCure Clifton, NJ\nPetCure Dallas Fort Worth\nPetCure Phoenix\nPetCure Pittsburgh\nPetCure San Antonio\nPetCure San Jose\nTraveling For Cancer Treatment\nPet Stories\nPet Parent Stories\nShare Your Pet Story\nFor Vets\nRefer a Patient\nComplimentary Imaging Reviews\nAbout Radiation Oncology\nPrimary Care Veterinarians\nB-Cell Lymphoma in Dogs\nNon-Cancerous Conditions\nPost Surgical Radiation\nClinical Information\nCase Studies\nNon-Urgent Questions\nVeterinary FAQ\nAbout\nHistory & Mission\nClinical Leadership\nBusiness Leadership\nContact\nPet Parents: Get Help Now!\nVeterinarians: Refer A Patient\nSearch PetCure Oncology\n833-738-4376\nPetCure Oncology Dallas Fort Worth\nPetCure Oncology is proud to announce its newest location in Mansfield, TX in the greater Dallas/Fort Worth areas.\nIn addition to the greater Dallas/Fort Worth area, we also welcome those from surrounding states like Louisiana and Oklahoma. No matter where you’re coming from, you’ll find that our Dallas/Fort Worth facility is a state-of-the-art facility, ready to help you and your pet.\nLocated in Mansfield, a suburb to the south of Dallas/Fort Worth, PetCure Oncology Dallas operates the radiation oncology service within\nThrive Pet Healthcare Specialists –  Mansfield\n, a 24-hour emergency and veterinary specialty center that is prepared to care for pets any time, day, or night. In addition to state-of-the-art medical oncology and radiation oncology services, this specialty hospital also provides 24/7 emergency care and orthopedics specialists.\nHow To Make An Appointment\nReach out to us at\n(817) 473-7838\n, or streamline your request by selecting one of the options below:\nPET PARENTS: GET HELP NOW!\nVETERINARIANS: REFER A PATIENT\nYour Care Team\nPetCure Radiation Oncologist:\nKaranbir Randhawa, DVM, DACVR (RO)\nDr. Randhawa is a board-certified Radiation Oncologist and will be spearheading the radiation oncology department at PetCure Oncology Dallas starting in February 2024. He is a distinguished graduate of the University of Wisconsin’s veterinary school where he also completed his residency. His foray into radiation oncology was sparked by an interest in both physics and technology.\nDr. Randhawa is committed to pushing the boundaries of veterinary medicine where he envisions continual advancements in treatment options. His passion for radiation oncology lies in exploring innovative applications of radiation and its various sources.\nWhen he’s not helping pet patients, Dr. Randhawa enjoys spending time with his cat, Cherry Berry, and his dogs, Thorin and Balin. During his spare time, you can find him playing basketball, boxing, or playing Warhammer 40K.\nLearn more about PetCure Oncology’s clinical specialists.\nThrive Medical Oncologist:\nMichelle\nLaRue\n, DVM, DACVIM (Oncology)\nDr.\nLaRue\nwas born and raised in the Dallas/Fort Worth area. Her love of veterinary medicine took her to Texas A&M University where she completed her undergraduate and veterinary school training. She completed a rotating internship at Auburn University and a specialty medical oncology internship from Louisiana State University. She completed her medical oncology residency and master’s degree at Auburn University which allowed her to become board-certified in medical oncology. She is drawn to developing treatments that are personalized, improve a patient’s quality of life and, to allow patients more quality time at home with their loved-ones.\nThrive Medical Oncologist:\nNatalie Christianson, DVM, DACVIM (Oncology)\nDr. Christianson attended veterinary school at Tufts University in Massachusetts. She pursued a rotating internship at the University of Wisconsin–Madison before returning to Tufts for an oncology clinical trials internship. She then attended the University of Georgia for her medical oncology residency. With four years of experience in oncology, Dr. Christianson brings passion and dedication to her care. Her approach centers on treating each patient as an individual, tailoring treatment plans to support not only the best medical outcomes, but also the best quality of life for her patients and their families. Dr. Christianson enjoys spending time at home with her wife, Jess, also a veterinarian, and their five cats (Schmitt, Freddie Mercury, JJ, Lenny, and Tuna). Together, they enjoy trying new breweries, tending to their vegetable garden, and spending time with family.\nRadiation Therapist:\nLynette P., RT(T)\nPractice Lead:\nAlexa R., LVT\nVeterinary Technician:\nCaitlin G., LVT\nVeterinary Technician:\nMatt H, LVT\nCSR/RC:\nAly S\n.\nTeam Email:\nPetCure.Dallas@ThrivePet.com\nProudly Serving the Dallas/Fort Worth Areas & Beyond\nWe’re excited to extend a warm welcome to patients from across Texas and surrounding areas to our Dallas/Fort Worth location. Our doors are open to everyone, whether you’re a local from the Dallas/Fort Worth area, or from farther away in neighboring towns or even neighboring states. Pet patients and their families visit us from all over including, but not limited to, these fantastic communities:\nAmarillo\nArlington\nAustin\nBurleson\nCiudad Juarez, Chihuahua, Mexico\nDallas\nDenton\nFort Worth\nGarland\nGranbury\nIrving\nNorman\nKilleen\nLubbock\nMansfield\nMidlothian\nOklahoma City, OK\nPlano\nShreveport, LA\nWaxahachie\nWichita Falls\nand surrounding areas\nIf You Are Traveling From Out-Of-Town\nWe want to make your visit to the Dallas/Fort Worth area as easy and stress-free as possible. If you would like\nassistance finding pet-friendly hotels and restaurants nearby\n, we are happy to help. Also, see our\nTips For Traveling With Your Pet For Cancer Treatment\n. If you have any other questions, simply ask one of our client service representatives.\nPRESS RELEASE:\nDallas-Fort Worth Area Pets Can Now Get Emergency & Cancer Care Under One Roof\nPetCure Oncology Dallas Fort Worth\n301 U.S. 287 Frontage Rd.\nMansfield, TX, 76063\nPhone: (817) 473-7838\nFax: (817) 473-2738\nEmail:\nPetcure.Dallas@ThrivePet.com\nWebsite:\npetcureoncology.com/locations/dallas-fort-worth/\nGet Directions\nMore Locations\nVeterinary Cancer Group\nPetCure Oncology San Antonio\nPetCure Oncology Clifton NJ\nPetCure Oncology Chicago\nPetCure Oncology Phoenix\nPetCure Oncology Pittsburgh\nPetCure Oncology San Jose\nPetCure Oncology Dallas Fort Worth\nMore Than 10,000 Pet Families Have Chosen PetCure Oncology For Their Dog Or Cat's Cancer Therapy. We Give Your Pet A Fighting Chance To Improve Their Quality Of Life.\nWe Understand. We Commit. We Will Help.\nPET PARENTS: GET HELP NOW!\nVETERINARIANS REFER A PATIENT\n833-738-4376\nSRS/SRT FAQ\nVets FAQ\nContact\nNews\nPress Room\nCareers\nFacebook\nInstagram\nTikTok\nLinkedIn\nSIGN UP FOR NEWSLETTER\nAt PetCure Oncology we are unconditionally committed to delivering industry-leading cancer care to pets and unwavering support to the families who love them. Pet families are given guidance, knowledge, and access to comprehensive and compassionate pet cancer care. Together with our pet patients and their families, we share in the cancer journey. We believe pet parents deserve the best clinical expertise and advanced treatment options for their pets.\nPrivacy Notice\n|\nTerms of Use\n|\nDisclaimer Notice\n|\nYour Privacy Choices\nCopyright ©2026\nPetCure Oncology\n. All Rights Reserved.\nNEED ANSWERS? WE'RE HERE FOR YOU.\nCall\n833-738-4376\nnow to speak with a member of the Pet Advocate Team.\nBACK TO TOP",
